{
  "id": "05998_keno",
  "headword": "{嫌悪|けんお}",
  "reading": "けんお",
  "part_of_speech": "noun, suru verb",
  "gloss": "disgust; loathing; aversion",
  "conjugation": {
    "type": "suru",
    "prefix": "{嫌悪|けんお}"
  },
  "definitions": [
    {
      "sense_number": 1,
      "gloss": "disgust; loathing; aversion",
      "explanation": "A strong feeling of dislike or repulsion toward something or someone. Stronger than simple dislike."
    }
  ],
  "examples": [
    {
      "id": "05998_keno_ex1",
      "japanese": "{暴力|ぼうりょく}を{嫌悪|けんお}する。",
      "english": "I loathe violence.",
      "notes": null,
      "has_audio": false,
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "05998_keno_ex2",
      "japanese": "{彼|かれ}の{態度|たいど}に{嫌悪感|けんおかん}を{抱|いだ}いた。",
      "english": "I felt disgust at his attitude.",
      "notes": null,
      "has_audio": false,
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "05998_keno_ex3",
      "japanese": "{自己|じこ}{嫌悪|けんお}に{陥|おちい}ることがある。",
      "english": "Sometimes I fall into self-loathing.",
      "notes": null,
      "has_audio": false,
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "05998_keno_ex4",
      "japanese": "{差別|さべつ}に{対|たい}する{嫌悪感|けんおかん}は{年々|ねんねん}{強|つよ}まっている。",
      "english": "The aversion toward discrimination has been growing stronger year by year.",
      "notes": null,
      "has_audio": false,
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "05998_keno_ex5",
      "japanese": "{失敗|しっぱい}した{自分|じぶん}が{嫌|いや}で、{自己|じこ}{嫌悪|けんお}に{苦|くる}しんだ{時期|じき}があった。",
      "english": "There was a period when I hated myself for failing and suffered from self-loathing.",
      "notes": null,
      "has_audio": false,
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ]
    }
  ],
  "notes": "{嫌悪|けんお} expresses strong dislike or revulsion — much stronger than {嫌|きら}い. It belongs to a formal or literary register and is common in written Japanese, news, and psychology.\n\nWORD FORMATION:\n{嫌|けん} (dislike) + {悪|お} (bad, loathe)\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {嫌悪感|けんおかん}: feeling of disgust\n- {嫌悪感|けんおかん}を{抱|いだ}く: to harbor disgust\n- {自己|じこ}{嫌悪|けんお}: self-loathing\n- {嫌悪|けんお}を{示|しめ}す: to show aversion\n\nCONTRAST:\n- {嫌|きら}い: dislike (casual, everyday)\n- {嫌悪|けんお}: loathing (formal, stronger)\n- {憎|にく}しみ: hatred (personal, emotional)\n- {軽蔑|けいべつ}: contempt (looking down on someone)",
